{
  "about": "The normative lock of the RFC 07 contract vectors (D8). A suite is normative only when the generator's source and an implementation independent of it agreed on every case. Each locked case is pinned by the SHA-256 of the canonical JSON of its id, input and expect (tools/check.py case_hash: Python json.dumps with sort_keys=True, separators (',', ':') and ensure_ascii=False, encoded as UTF-8), so neither the input nor the expected value of a locked case can change. Locked entries never change or disappear: a change needs a new wire version and a new suite. Entries are added only by tools/check.py --promote, which locks only cases the oracle reproduced in that run; CI also requires the oracle to reproduce, in the same run, every entry added relative to the base commit. Informative values (for example the GROWN/1 commitment of shdccp2_record) are outside the lock. CC0-1.0, see LICENSE.",
